<title>BELGIUM: MILLENNIUM SWITCH TO COST BELGIUM 19 BLN BFR.</title>
<headline>MILLENNIUM SWITCH TO COST BELGIUM 19 BLN BFR.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Adapting computer systems to the millennium change will cost Belgian companies and public authorities at least 19 billion francs, Economy Minister Elio di Rupo said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He said a poll among public administrations and professional organisations showed that many groups were not yet adequately prepared to switch their computers to the year 2000.</p>
<p>Many existing computer systems only use two digits to indicate the year, in order to save computer memory.</p>
<p>Di Rupo said the total cost would be much higher, as the estimate was based only on partial replies from the federations.</p>
